    title: "2026年3月，十四届全国人大四次会议民生主题记者会披露社区养老服务扩面计划，全国老年助餐点已达8.2万家。",
    units: 358,
    text: "2026年3月，十四届全国人大四次会议举行民生主题记者会。会上介绍，全国老年助餐点已达8.2万家，每天为400余万人次老年人提供助餐服务，初步形成覆盖城乡的助餐服务网络。与此同时，有关部门提出，在“十五五”时期力争将社区养老服务机构和设施覆盖率提高到70%以上。\n\n在具体做法上，各地因地制宜探索不同路径。有的城市在社区建设嵌入式养老服务中心，把助餐、助医、助急等服务送到老人家门口；有的地方引入专业团队运营社区食堂，针对行动不便的高龄、独居老人推出送餐上门服务；一些农村地区则利用闲置校舍建设助餐点，通过多元筹资维持日常运转。部分社区食堂还向“全龄共享”转型，老年人享受优惠价格，其他年龄段居民按市场价就餐，以此增加客流、实现微利可持续运营。\n\n这些变化背后有一个共同思路：养老服务不能只靠政府“输血”，还需要政府、市场和社会多方协同，建立长效运营机制。从一顿热饭开始，越来越多的老年人在家门口就能享受到稳定、可负担的日常服务。",
    reference: "In March 2026, a press conference on livelihood issues was held during the fourth session of the 14th National People’s Congress. It was announced that China now has 82,000 meal assistance sites for the elderly, serving over 4 million senior citizens daily, with a basic service network covering both urban and rural areas. Meanwhile, authorities set a goal of raising the coverage rate of community elderly care institutions and facilities to over 70 percent during the 15th Five-Year Plan period.\n\nIn practice, different regions have explored different approaches suited to local conditions. Some cities have built embedded elderly care centers in communities, bringing meal assistance, medical support and emergency help to the doorstep of seniors. Some have invited professional teams to run community canteens and introduced home delivery for frail, elderly people living alone. In some rural areas, unused school buildings have been converted into meal service sites, with funding from multiple sources to cover daily operations. Some community canteens have also shifted toward serving all age groups, offering discounted prices for seniors while charging market rates for others, so as to increase foot traffic and keep the business running on thin margins.\n\nBehind these changes is a shared idea: elderly care cannot rely on government funding alone. It requires coordination among the government, the market and society to build a sustainable operating model. Starting with a warm meal, more and more seniors can now access stable, affordable daily services close to home.",
