    reference: "Jinkeyuan Community in Yuhua District, Changsha, was built in 1963. Covering only 0.1 square kilometers, it has 28 old residential buildings housing more than 1,200 households and over 5,000 residents, with people aged 60 and above accounting for 30 percent. Most of the buildings were constructed before the 1990s, with weak infrastructure and incomplete facilities. At the end of 2019, the community completed the transfer of water, electricity, heating and property management services and came under local administration.\n\nIn 2022, the community launched a renovation of its old residential areas. Supported by a pilot program for complete community development, it invested a total of 128 million yuan in 38 livelihood projects. An old single workers’ dormitory was converted into 216 youth apartments, rented at 1,000 to 1,500 yuan per month, with an occupancy rate of 100 percent. The community also revitalized existing buildings to create a comprehensive elderly care service center and a senior sports and wellness center, adding 973 meters of accessible handrails and 366 folding chairs in stairwells. An old factory was turned into a vocational training base for people with disabilities, the kindergarten added childcare classes, and a multifunctional children’s activity area was built. Twenty-three elevators were installed in residential buildings, stair handrails were reinforced, roofs were waterproofed, and all pipelines were replaced.\n\nIn July this year, the Ministry of Housing and Urban-Rural Development released the first batch of “Complete Community Construction Case Studies,” selecting 10 national models. Jinkeyuan was the only community in Hunan to be included. Today, the community has formed a “15-minute convenience life circle” covering 29 types of basic services and 28 types of quality-of-life improvements, with resident satisfaction above 95 percent. One elderly resident who had moved away to live with her children returned after seeing the changes. Dozens of other seniors have done the same.",
