    reference: "In September 2026, a community restaurant opened in Chongxi Community, Chongwenmenwai Subdistrict, Beijing, bringing what residents call the “taste of happiness” to their doorstep. The community on Chongwenmen West Street has a high proportion of elderly residents, and many who live alone or whose children have moved away face the difficulty of cooking or simply making do with meals. The community made building the “Happiness Canteen” a key livelihood project, and the carefully designed restaurant won praise as soon as it opened.\n\nThe canteen focuses on meals that are “low in salt, oil and sugar, and soft and easy to chew,” while also catering to the tastes of residents of all ages. The menu is varied, with a balance of meat and vegetables, and rotates daily. Lunch offers 12 dishes, dinner 10 to 12, and the menu changes every day. One resident in his eighties, among the first to try the food, was full of praise: “I’m old and cooking is hard work, and my children are busy with their jobs. Now I can just go downstairs and have a hot meal. The food is soft, the price is reasonable, and it’s so thoughtful.”\n\nThe canteen is not just a place to eat but also a “living room” for neighbors to meet. Residents line up in an orderly way and dine politely, creating a warm and friendly atmosphere. A community official said the canteen will continue to be guided by residents’ needs and improve its service, letting a “small canteen” support “big livelihood” and spread warmth to every corner of the community.",
