    units: 424,
    text: "2026年9月，第23届中国—东盟博览会在广西南宁举办。本届东博会的一个重要背景，是中国—东盟自贸区3.0版升级议定书正式签署。与过去以货物贸易为主的合作不同，升级版将合作领域拓展到数字经济、绿色经济等新兴方向。\n\n博览会期间，首次设立了东盟国家需求展区，首次举行了中国—东盟人工智能供需对接会，还首次举办了面向特定国家的“出口中国”专场活动。来自多个国家的企业代表在对接会上洽谈合作，现场达成了一批合作意向。中方企业展示了在人工智能、新一代信息技术等领域的方案，东盟方面则带来了具体的市场需求清单，双方按需对接，效率明显提高。\n\n另一个值得关注的变化发生在物流通道上。就在东博会期间，平陆运河实现全线通航。这条运河把中国西南内陆与北部湾港口直接连接起来，使西南腹地与东盟之间的运输距离大幅缩短，物流成本随之降低。过去需要绕行其他路线的货物，现在可以经这条新通道更快出海。\n\n从贸易到投资，从数字经济到物流通道，中国与东盟之间的合作正在变得更加具体和务实。正如一位参会代表所说，合作的关键不在于签了多少文件，而在于这些文件能不能变成一条路、一批货、一个项目。",
    reference: "In September 2026, the 23rd China-ASEAN Expo was held in Nanning, Guangxi. An important backdrop to this year’s expo was the formal signing of the Protocol to Upgrade the China-ASEAN Free Trade Area to Version 3.0. Unlike past cooperation focused mainly on trade in goods, the upgraded version extends collaboration into emerging areas such as the digital economy and green economy.\n\nDuring the expo, a pavilion showcasing ASEAN countries’ demand was set up for the first time. A China-ASEAN matchmaking session on artificial intelligence supply and demand was also held for the first time, along with a dedicated “Export to China” event for a specific country. Business representatives from multiple countries held talks at the matchmaking session, reaching a number of cooperation intentions on site. Chinese companies presented solutions in artificial intelligence and next-generation information technology, while ASEAN counterparts brought specific lists of market needs. The two sides matched according to demand, making the process notably more efficient.\n\nAnother notable change took place in logistics. During the expo, the Pinglu Canal opened to full navigation. The canal directly connects China’s southwestern interior with ports on the Beibu Gulf, significantly shortening transport distances between the southwestern hinterland and ASEAN and reducing logistics costs. Goods that previously had to take other routes can now reach the sea faster through this new channel.\n\nFrom trade to investment, from the digital economy to logistics corridors, cooperation between China and ASEAN is becoming more concrete and practical. As one delegate put it, what matters is not how many documents are signed, but whether those documents can turn into a road, a shipment or a project.",
